    "instruction": "Improve the whole ordinary program using the task specification and measured examples. You may freely refactor any function, change interfaces or retained state, add/remove helpers, or replace the whole implementation. Diagnose the actual cause; a local edit is not required. Preserve a correct program when no useful change is needed.",
    "current_program": "def investigate(context, acquire):\n    values = context[\"values\"]\n    n = len(values)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    # Infer polynomial p(x)=a*x+b*x*x+c*x*x*x from single-element cases.\n    # For single element x, contribution = p(x), then 4 cumulative passes\n    # on a length-1 list leave it unchanged. So expected = p(x).\n    # From calibration: p(1)=0, p(2)=6, p(-1)=0.\n    # Solve: a+b+c=0; 2a+4b+8c=6; -a+b-c=0.\n    # From a+b+c=0 and -a+b-c=0 => b=0, a+c=0 => c=-a.\n    # 2a+8c=6 => 2a-8a=6 => -6a=6 => a=-1, c=1, b=0.\n    # p(x) = -x + x*x*x\n    def p(x):\n        return -x + x*x*x\n    # Build contribution list. Need to infer g and preceding mode.\n    # Use development examples to fit. Try all g in {-2,-1,1,2} and modes.\n    # Also number of passes 1..4.\n    best = None\n    best_score = -1\n    # We'll test candidate parameters against known examples embedded.\n    # But we must not hardcode outputs; instead we can use calibration+development\n    # as training data available in context? No, context only has values.\n    # So we must pick the correct parameters by reasoning from examples.\n    # Let's derive from examples manually via code logic that fits all.\n    # We'll implement a search over parameters using the provided examples\n    # as a fixed training set (allowed: they are part of task spec).\n    train = [\n        ([], 0), ([0], 0), ([1], 0), ([2], 6), ([-1], 0),\n        ([1,0], 0), ([0,1], 0), ([1,1], -1), ([1,0,0], 0),\n        ([1,1,1], -5), ([1,2,1], 9), ([2,1,0], 30),\n        ([-2,-3], -48), ([3,0,0], 144), ([3,3,3,3], 345),\n        ([-3,3,-3,3,-3], -99), ([-3,0,0,-2,0,0], -576),\n        ([1,-3], -21), ([0,3,2], 72), ([0,0,-3,0], -72),\n        ([-2,-2,-2,-2,-2], -350), ([-4,4,-4,4,-4,4], -368),\n        ([-1,0], 0), ([-1,0,2], 8), ([-1,-3,0,1], -158),\n        ([0,0,0,3,0], 72), ([-1,-1,-1,-1,-1,-1], -70),\n        ([-2,2], -8), ([3,0,0,2], 240), ([-1,1,0,3,0], 82),\n        ([0,0,0,0,0,4], 60), ([-1,-1], -1), ([-2,2,-2], -12),\n        ([-3,0,0,-4], -312), ([0,0,0,0,3], 24),\n        ([0,1,0,2,-3,-1], -21),\n    ]\n    def simulate(vals, g, mode, passes):\n        m = len(vals)\n        if m == 0:\n            return 0\n        contrib = []\n        for i in range(m):\n            x = vals[i]\n            base = p(x)\n            if i == 0:\n                contrib.append(base)\n            else:\n                if mode == 0:\n                    prev = vals[i-1]\n                else:\n                    prev = sum(vals[:i])\n                contrib.append(base + g * x * prev)\n        cur = contrib\n        for _ in range(passes):\n            nxt = []\n            s = 0\n            for v in cur:\n                s += v\n                nxt.append(s)\n            cur = nxt\n        return cur[-1]\n    candidates = []\n    for g in (-2, -1, 1, 2):\n        for mode in (0, 1):\n            for passes in (1, 2, 3, 4):\n                candidates.append((g, mode, passes))\n    for g, mode, passes in candidates:\n        score = 0\n        for vals, exp in train:\n            if simulate(vals, g, mode, passes) == exp:\n                score += 1\n        if score > best_score:\n            best_score = score\n            best = (g, mode, passes)\n    g, mode, passes = best\n    return simulate(values, g, mode, passes)\n",
